  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Let the vectors $v$ and $w$ be orthogonal. \nIf $|u\\cdot v{|}^{2}+5\u2016v+w{\u2016}^{2}=101$ and $\u2016u\u2016=\u2016w\u2016=2$, then what is the minimum possible value of $\u2016v\u2016?$",
  "worked_solution": "First, using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}101 & ={|u\\cdot v|}^{2}+5\u2016v+w{\u2016}^{2} \\\\  & \\le {\u2016u{\u2016}^{2}\\cdot \u2016v\u2016}^{2}+5\u2016v+w{\u2016}^{2} \\\\  & ={2}^{2}\\cdot \u2016v{\u2016}^{2}+5\u2016v+w{\u2016}^{2} \\\\  & =4\u2016v{\u2016}^{2}+5\u2016v+w{\u2016}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $v\u22a5w$, using the Pythagorean theorem, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\u2016v{\u2016}^{2}+5\u2016v+w{\u2016}^{2} & =4\u2016v{\u2016}^{2}+5(\u2016v{\u2016}^{2}+\u2016w{\u2016}^{2}) \\\\  & =4\u2016v{\u2016}^{2}+5(\u2016v{\u2016}^{2}+{2}^{2}) \\\\  & =9\u2016v{\u2016}^{2}+20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining the two steps above, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}101 & \\le 9\u2016v\u2016+20 \\\\ 81 & \\le 9\u2016v{\u2016}^{2} \\\\ 9 & \\le \u2016v{\u2016}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $9\\le \u2016v{\u2016}^{2}$ implies that $3\\le \u2016v\u2016.$ Notice that we disregard the negative solutions since the norm can't be negative.\n\nTherefore, the minimum possible value of $\u2016v\u2016$ is $3.$",
